  "notes": "Form-366 block_13 fields were garbled in input ('to'/'ICES'); reconstructed system=BF (ADS), component=RV (relief valve) from narrative EIIS codes. Cause code officially TBD/provisional per form fields despite narrative clearly attributing root cause to out-of-spec vendor plunger; category kept as 'provisional' per rule 4. Bracket tilt and plunger oversizing are modeled as two parallel failure modes converging on plunger rubbing, since narrative describes them as distinct defects (bent bracket tolerated in prior cycles; plunger width was the triggering out-of-spec condition). No BACKED_UP_BY edges emitted: LPCI/Core Spray and other ADS valves are discussed only as design-basis/system-design context or as separately-tested valves, not as backups operable specifically during this valve's inoperability window in a way meeting rule 6's strict test; other 4 ADS valves stroked successfully but this is capacity confirmation, not an explicit backup-during-event statement, so treated as note only. Previous occurrence LER key preserved exactly as '254/2010-001-00' per report text."
